WEBVTT

00:04.980 --> 00:07.670
So even you air out your 
futon mattress properly, huh, Ron?

00:07.950 --> 00:08.740
Wait...

00:08.740 --> 00:10.910
It's so long!

00:13.500 --> 00:15.370
What a surprise.

00:15.370 --> 00:17.520
Had no idea you aired out 
the Floor of Indolence.

00:17.520 --> 00:20.210
I drop it sometimes too, 
so don't try this at home.

00:20.210 --> 00:22.080
Yeah, never in my life will I do this.

00:29.930 --> 00:31.800
You look unhappy, Toto.

00:31.800 --> 00:33.940
It's just... I was going to say,

00:33.940 --> 00:37.210
"You've been weird since we came 
back from the observatory."

00:37.210 --> 00:40.020
But thinking about it, 
you've always been weird.

00:40.020 --> 00:43.710
That means <i>you're</i> the one 
who's being weird, Toto.

00:43.710 --> 00:44.400
What?

00:45.440 --> 00:46.850
Well, you might be right.

00:47.180 --> 00:49.360
But only because you're
 saying strange things.

00:49.690 --> 00:53.070
The boat carrying the 
observatory murderer sank,

00:53.070 --> 00:57.240
the crew is all missing, and you claim it 
wasn't an accident. Stuff like that.

00:57.240 --> 00:59.830
Yeah, it's the only explanation
 I can think of.

01:00.700 --> 01:05.480
Whoever put this mark on my neck during
the Bloody Training Incident five years ago

01:05.480 --> 01:07.050
also sank that boat.

01:07.050 --> 01:10.250
If that's true, 
I'm amazed you can stay so calm.

01:10.250 --> 01:12.220
Isn't the terror creeping up on you?

01:12.220 --> 01:14.510
Running around in a panic 
won't help, will it?

01:14.510 --> 01:18.470
As I take the appropriate measures, 
I'll still enjoy my everyday life.

01:18.470 --> 01:20.400
Must be nice to be so carefree.

01:25.480 --> 01:27.210
Oh, I'm sorry!

01:27.210 --> 01:29.650
Except... it wasn't there earlier, was it?

01:29.650 --> 01:32.580
On a similar subject, 
this wandered into my suitcase.

01:32.580 --> 01:34.780
It's a souvenir from Nandan Island, right?

01:34.780 --> 01:36.970
I'm sure Amamiya-kun will be thrilled.

01:36.970 --> 01:38.490
Really? You think so?

01:38.490 --> 01:40.250
Guaranteed to make her laugh!

01:40.250 --> 01:41.530
Right?!

01:54.230 --> 01:57.560
Ron    Kamonohashi's

01:54.230 --> 01:57.560
<i>Forbidden\h\h\h
</i>Deductions

03:14.470 --> 03:16.880
Amamiya-senpai, I brought you this souvenir.

03:14.470 --> 03:17.800
<b>Investigation Division 1</b>

03:16.880 --> 03:17.800
Thanks.

03:17.800 --> 03:21.140
<b>#10   The Case of the Poisoned Latte</b>

03:18.380 --> 03:19.760
Now then, Isshiki...

03:19.760 --> 03:21.140
<i>She's ignoring it!</i>

03:21.140 --> 03:23.100
I have a job for you.

03:23.100 --> 03:24.100
Huh?

03:25.520 --> 03:29.770
She didn't give me any details. 
I wonder what this job is.

03:27.810 --> 03:29.770
<b>Conference Room</b>

03:27.810 --> 03:29.770
<b>No. 3</b>

03:32.980 --> 03:34.810
It's really him...

03:36.340 --> 03:37.400
Lime Weekly

03:36.340 --> 03:37.400
Reporter Monki Chikori

03:39.620 --> 03:41.060
Nice to meet you!

03:41.060 --> 03:44.210
My name is Monki Chikori. 
I'm from <i>Lime Weekly</i>.

03:46.030 --> 03:48.580
I'm Isshiki from Investigation Division 1.

03:48.580 --> 03:50.910
So... you're a reporter?

03:50.910 --> 03:54.500
Yes! I'm here to shadow you 
for a day, Detective Isshiki.

03:54.500 --> 03:56.720
Y-You're shadowing <i>me</i>?

03:56.720 --> 03:57.740
That's right.

03:57.740 --> 04:01.300
For the "People to Watch" column of our 
newest issue. I'd be much obliged!

04:01.300 --> 04:02.760
"People to Watch"?

04:02.760 --> 04:05.360
Don't you normally cover 
entertainers or athletes

04:05.360 --> 04:06.910
for something like that?

04:06.910 --> 04:10.750
After cases like the serial 
drownings in the metropolis

04:10.750 --> 04:12.460
and the Hand Collector murders,

04:12.460 --> 04:15.760
I wouldn't want anyone other
 than the man who solved them.

04:15.760 --> 04:20.070
But that wasn't in any of the papers.
 How did you know I solved those?

04:20.070 --> 04:21.530
Because I'm completely enamored!

04:21.530 --> 04:22.740
En—

04:22.740 --> 04:24.700
Oh, I don't mean that in a weird way!

04:25.610 --> 04:29.930
I was kidnapped as a child, you see.

04:31.380 --> 04:35.100
The man who valiantly
 cracked the case and saved me

04:35.100 --> 04:36.590
was a police detective.

04:38.090 --> 04:41.740
Ever since then, detectives 
have been heroes in my eyes.

04:41.740 --> 04:44.010
That's why I became a reporter.

04:44.010 --> 04:45.990
It's also why, in my own way,

04:45.990 --> 04:48.870
I try to investigate unsolved cases 
and impossible crimes.

04:48.870 --> 04:52.800
And I've watched you neatly unravel
 one after another, Detective Isshiki.

04:52.800 --> 04:54.860
You're a hero among heroes.

04:54.860 --> 04:57.070
You're a god to me!

04:57.070 --> 04:58.470
<i>A god?!</i>

04:58.970 --> 05:00.860
<i>She's an odd one.</i>

05:00.860 --> 05:04.010
<i>She's under the mistaken impression 
I cracked those cases,</i>

05:04.010 --> 05:06.660
<i>but I can't expose Ron, 
so I'm kinda stuck here.</i>

05:06.660 --> 05:09.850
You're absolutely free to decline
 if it'd be imposing.

05:09.850 --> 05:12.280
I understand it's a lot to ask.

05:12.280 --> 05:14.710
I'm incredibly grateful just to have met you!

05:15.130 --> 05:16.720
Honestly!

05:17.340 --> 05:19.480
No, it's fine!

05:19.800 --> 05:22.630
I'm just not assigned
 to anything at the moment...

05:22.630 --> 05:23.550
Amazing!

05:23.550 --> 05:26.260
So they're reserving you
 for the next big case?

05:26.630 --> 05:29.060
That's the ace detective
 of Division 1 for you!

05:29.060 --> 05:30.980
<i>The misunderstanding is snowballing!</i>

05:37.920 --> 05:41.340
Seeing a great detective at work
 is just so moving for me.

05:41.340 --> 05:44.380
So, you take time to keep
 all the paperwork in order too?

05:44.380 --> 05:45.910
Oh, y-yeah.

05:45.910 --> 05:48.620
<i>That's actually the bulk of my job.</i>

05:48.620 --> 05:51.530
<i>I want to get this over with
before she wises up, but...</i>

05:56.280 --> 05:58.520
I've just got more paperwork after this,

05:58.520 --> 06:01.510
so how about an interview 
over a quick cup of tea?

06:01.510 --> 06:02.760
Would that work...?

06:02.760 --> 06:05.260
I'd be honored to join you for a drink!

06:13.940 --> 06:16.200
I'll have a hot cocoa.

06:16.200 --> 06:18.760
I'll have an iced coffee. Black.

06:18.760 --> 06:19.760
We don't have that.

06:19.760 --> 06:20.400
What?

06:20.860 --> 06:22.860
The only black thing here is sugar syrup.

06:22.860 --> 06:23.780
Ron—

06:23.780 --> 06:24.580
What?

06:24.580 --> 06:27.100
My name is Chasaku Kamokyuu.

06:27.100 --> 06:29.330
There is no "ro" or "n" in it.

06:29.330 --> 06:31.290
<i>That's definitely Ron!</i>

06:31.290 --> 06:34.530
A coffee shop that doesn't do coffee?

06:34.530 --> 06:36.630
Can I have a word with you over there?

06:37.430 --> 06:41.090
That's a great detective for you! 
Admonishing him so resolutely...

06:41.090 --> 06:42.680
What are you doing?

06:42.680 --> 06:43.460
Helping.

06:43.460 --> 06:44.230
What?

06:44.230 --> 06:49.300
I'm here to lecture the owner on how to 
make my special black sugar syrup latte.

06:49.300 --> 06:51.550
You sure have a lot of free time.

06:54.230 --> 06:57.020
Only because someone's not bringing me work.

06:57.020 --> 06:57.730
Uh-oh.

06:57.730 --> 06:59.420
Got anything unsolved cases?

06:59.420 --> 07:00.940
None today either.

07:01.570 --> 07:04.270
Are you on a date? With that reporter lady?

07:04.270 --> 07:06.200
Huh? How'd you know she's a reporter?

07:06.200 --> 07:07.440
It's simple.

07:08.030 --> 07:11.880
When she entered the cafe, the first thing 
she checked was the magazine rack.

07:11.880 --> 07:16.210
And the fact that the front of her shoes 
are scuffed suggests she runs a lot.

07:16.210 --> 07:18.290
Her phone case is also stuffed with cards.

07:18.290 --> 07:19.670
Another telltale sign.

07:19.670 --> 07:21.430
I see.

07:21.430 --> 07:24.340
But this is for work! 
She's really got the wrong idea...

07:24.340 --> 07:25.770
How about this place?

07:25.770 --> 07:27.180
I think it'll do, yeah?

07:27.550 --> 07:29.410
I like it too.

07:29.760 --> 07:31.810
It's pretty fancy, isn't it?

07:31.810 --> 07:34.440
I'll go get a shot of the sign outside.

07:34.440 --> 07:35.730
Got it.

07:35.730 --> 07:37.750
We'll go ahead and order.

07:37.750 --> 07:39.260
So, what do you want?

07:39.260 --> 07:40.940
I'll have a caffè latte.

07:40.940 --> 07:42.900
Me too! I'll have the same!

07:42.900 --> 07:44.000
Welcome.

07:44.000 --> 07:46.060
Um, three lattes, please.

07:46.060 --> 07:47.550
Coming right up.

07:47.550 --> 07:50.370
We're first come, first served,
so it'll be just a moment.

07:52.830 --> 07:54.790
Here you are. One cocoa and one black.

07:54.790 --> 07:57.780
Black? It isn't straight sugar syrup, is it?

07:57.780 --> 07:59.560
You really think I'd do that?

07:59.560 --> 08:01.170
O-Of course not.

08:01.170 --> 08:02.650
I thinned it with water.

08:05.170 --> 08:06.620
Chasaku-san, was it?

08:06.620 --> 08:07.950
Chasaku Kamokyuu.

08:07.950 --> 08:09.760
Are you seriously working here?

08:28.650 --> 08:29.860
Done.

08:30.200 --> 08:32.070
Here you are. Three caffè lattes.

08:32.570 --> 08:34.280
Wow!

08:34.280 --> 08:36.180
When'd you learn such an impressive skill?

08:36.180 --> 08:40.000
The most important thing is drawing out
the platypus within the latte.

08:40.000 --> 08:41.120
Nobody asked.

08:41.120 --> 08:43.090
What an adorable duck!

08:44.550 --> 08:46.000
A d-d...

08:46.470 --> 08:47.840
Need a hand?

08:47.840 --> 08:49.370
I'm good!

08:49.730 --> 08:51.740
A d-duck?

08:53.000 --> 08:54.440
Don't mind me.

08:55.430 --> 08:56.810
Huh? Did you take my picture?

08:56.810 --> 08:57.870
I did.

08:57.870 --> 08:59.390
Are you doing a report on him?

08:59.390 --> 09:02.850
Yes. He's giving me incredibly 
valuable experience.

09:02.850 --> 09:04.150
Got questions for him?

09:04.150 --> 09:04.770
Hey.

09:04.770 --> 09:06.070
Of course!

09:06.070 --> 09:10.280
I'm going to write an article about
 the impossible cases he's solved.

09:11.490 --> 09:14.580
Tch, what a mess. I didn't realize 
she was a crime reporter.

09:18.660 --> 09:19.680
Help yourself.

09:19.680 --> 09:22.110
A sample of our black sugar
 syrup latte on the house!

09:22.110 --> 09:23.880
That is <i>not</i> a sample size!

09:23.880 --> 09:25.840
Y-You! Come with me a sec.

09:25.840 --> 09:27.410
There's no need to thank me.

09:27.410 --> 09:28.480
Get over here!

09:31.760 --> 09:33.480
What are you playing at?!

09:33.480 --> 09:36.750
Crime reporters can be sources
of critical intel on hard cases.

09:36.750 --> 09:39.500
You need to build 
a good relationship with her.

09:39.500 --> 09:40.230
What?

09:40.230 --> 09:42.940
All I can do right now is help set the stage!

09:42.940 --> 09:44.440
Wait! Hold it!

09:45.260 --> 09:48.590
Just between us, we also serve 
soba-restaurant-style curry!

09:48.590 --> 09:50.650
Then this isn't just a café anymore!

09:51.900 --> 09:55.290
Will you please stop causing 
problems for Detective Isshiki?

09:55.290 --> 09:58.870
His time incredibly precious. 
Too precious to waste on me, even!

09:59.540 --> 10:01.610
You think that highly of him?

10:02.000 --> 10:03.960
I like you.

10:03.960 --> 10:05.890
Where did that come from?

10:05.890 --> 10:07.170
Now, now...

10:12.340 --> 10:13.180
Julie?

10:15.520 --> 10:16.640
Miss?!

10:16.640 --> 10:17.640
Wh-What's wrong?

10:18.610 --> 10:20.110
Call an ambulance.

10:20.110 --> 10:20.990
All right.

10:21.850 --> 10:23.310
And the police.

10:23.310 --> 10:24.270
What?

10:25.040 --> 10:26.230
It was poison.

10:39.410 --> 10:44.840
We discovered a cyanide capsule
in the deceased woman's cup.

10:44.840 --> 10:46.120
I see.

10:47.000 --> 10:48.840
Excuse me.

10:48.840 --> 10:50.920
Don't worry. I will avenge you.

10:50.920 --> 10:52.220
Wha—Hey!

10:52.220 --> 10:53.710
Please move aside!

10:53.710 --> 10:55.910
Crime scenes are a
 great detective's battlefield,

10:55.910 --> 10:58.350
and this one is Detective Isshiki's specialty.

10:58.350 --> 11:00.670
So he's a great detective, is he?

11:00.670 --> 11:02.810
He's solved a number of difficult cases.

11:02.810 --> 11:05.060
He's a super sleuth to those in the know!

11:05.060 --> 11:07.520
<i>There she goes again with the praise!</i>

11:07.520 --> 11:10.280
I see. Well, that is heartening.

11:10.280 --> 11:12.720
Even a suspect like me 
is glad he's on the case.

11:12.720 --> 11:14.030
What? You're...

11:14.030 --> 11:15.110
A suspect?

11:15.110 --> 11:20.440
Yes, because only three people had a chance
 to put poison in this woman's coffee.

11:20.940 --> 11:22.680
Me, who made the caffè latte,

11:22.680 --> 11:25.550
and the two girls who were sitting with her.

11:29.790 --> 11:33.260
The question is who poisoned
 the drink and how.

11:34.710 --> 11:36.340
No need to worry.

11:38.630 --> 11:41.970
Detective Isshiki will neatly solve this case!

11:44.220 --> 11:45.230
Wha?

11:49.230 --> 11:52.440
I'm sure you're uneasy with someone 
like me covering this, but as a reporter,

11:52.440 --> 11:55.600
I'll do all I can to write 
a good article about your work!

11:55.600 --> 11:56.400
Um, I...

11:56.400 --> 12:00.670
I should mention that the cases 
of the giant snowman in Kushiro

12:00.670 --> 12:03.250
and the assassination 
of the eight-headed serpent in Izumo

12:03.250 --> 12:04.490
are among those I've covered.

12:04.490 --> 12:06.880
Those are famously complex cases!

12:06.880 --> 12:10.670
You're a very promising crime reporter.
 What's your name?

12:10.670 --> 12:12.710
Monki Chikori.

12:13.920 --> 12:16.380
From now on, 
regardless of where the case occurs,

12:16.380 --> 12:18.820
Detective Isshiki should be your first call.

12:18.820 --> 12:19.630
What?

12:19.630 --> 12:23.350
<i>He's trying to bag cases from all over 
the country through her connections!</i>

12:23.350 --> 12:25.560
You should watch him work today, too!

12:25.560 --> 12:27.060
Why are you saying all this?

12:27.060 --> 12:28.520
<i>She's got a point.</i>

12:33.310 --> 12:35.090
I'm Isshiki with the Metro PD.

12:35.090 --> 12:36.970
I'd like a word with the three of you.

12:36.970 --> 12:40.690
We believe the culprit was someone
with access to the victim's cup.

12:40.690 --> 12:44.970
So I'd like to know what you were all
 doing at the time of the incident.

12:44.970 --> 12:46.330
We'll start with the server.

12:46.330 --> 12:50.280
I had just poured the perfect latte,
but something was strange.

12:50.280 --> 12:50.790
What?

12:50.790 --> 12:54.350
My platypus latte art was mistaken for a duck.
A truly bizarre phenomenon.

12:54.350 --> 12:55.750
You really hold a grudge!

12:57.070 --> 12:59.840
Next is Hayami-san who carried the lattes.

12:59.840 --> 13:01.000
Sure.

13:01.550 --> 13:05.220
When I took our lattes over
 to the table, Julie...

13:05.220 --> 13:07.630
Let's snap a pic with the three of us!

13:07.630 --> 13:09.770
Okay, I'm taking it!

13:11.480 --> 13:14.890
After that, I took a phone call.

13:14.890 --> 13:17.370
Sorry, it's the manager 
from my part-time job.

13:17.370 --> 13:18.760
Hello, this is Hayami.

13:18.760 --> 13:21.000
I'm gonna take some 
photos around the café.

13:21.000 --> 13:22.950
Okay. I'll wait here.

13:22.950 --> 13:25.450
I wasn't on the phone long.

13:26.360 --> 13:28.820
Sorry about that. I know I kept you waiting.

13:28.820 --> 13:29.830
It's okay.

13:29.830 --> 13:31.260
Well, let's drink up!

13:31.260 --> 13:34.430
When I got back to my seat, 
Julie was the first one to take a cup.

13:34.430 --> 13:36.890
Then she drank it and collapsed.

13:38.340 --> 13:44.270
In other words, the only people who could 
have poisoned the drink were me,

13:44.270 --> 13:46.330
Hayami-kun who carried the lattes,

13:46.330 --> 13:49.810
and Tamada-kun who was left alone with them.

13:49.810 --> 13:52.660
Don't steal Detective Isshiki's lines!

13:52.660 --> 13:53.810
B-But...

13:54.150 --> 13:56.730
I don't think it was you, Kamokyuu-san.

13:56.730 --> 13:59.120
You couldn't have known who'd take which cup,

13:59.120 --> 14:01.960
and I see no motive for you to kill at random.

14:01.960 --> 14:04.010
Even if you wanted her dead,

14:04.010 --> 14:09.120
it would've been nigh impossible to determine
which cup would end up in front of her.

14:09.120 --> 14:10.860
H-How inspiring!

14:10.860 --> 14:14.210
To think I get to witness Detective
Isshiki's godly deductions in person!

14:14.210 --> 14:17.170
Indeed, I can see growth 
in his deductive abilities.

14:17.170 --> 14:18.890
Who do you think you are, exactly?

14:18.890 --> 14:20.920
Um, it wasn't like that.

14:20.920 --> 14:23.130
Right? I remember it too.

14:23.520 --> 14:27.850
Julie didn't take the cup in front of her.
She took one from the other side of the tray.

14:28.680 --> 14:29.640
What did you say?

14:29.640 --> 14:33.980
So how did the culprit get her to take 
the poisoned cup in the back?

14:37.690 --> 14:40.900
Ah, pardon me. Thank you for your testimony.

14:40.900 --> 14:45.380
For now, I'll use your accounts 
to begin sorting out the situation.

14:45.380 --> 14:47.150
Bear with us a little longer.

14:51.840 --> 14:54.740
There was no way to control the victim,

14:54.740 --> 14:56.520
so maybe it was some kind of trick.

14:56.520 --> 15:00.910
Too bad we don't have the latte anymore.

15:00.910 --> 15:02.250
Detective Isshiki.

15:03.050 --> 15:04.490
You dropped this.

15:04.490 --> 15:06.790
Huh? Thank you.

15:14.980 --> 15:16.190
Memo

15:14.980 --> 15:16.190
The victim's social media and the reporter's photos

15:16.190 --> 15:17.610
Oh, that's it!

15:17.610 --> 15:20.150
There may be evidence 
on Julie's social media!

15:20.150 --> 15:22.650
H-How clever! 
As expected of Detective Isshiki!

15:22.650 --> 15:25.180
Could I see the photos you took as well?

15:25.180 --> 15:28.110
O-Oh, of course! 
Sorry I didn't think of that sooner.

15:28.110 --> 15:31.160
I really only took shots of you, 
Detective Isshiki,

15:31.160 --> 15:35.840
but I do have one photo of the lattes 
the ladies ordered on the counter.

15:35.840 --> 15:37.330
That's a huge help!

15:37.330 --> 15:39.600
My lattes truly were perfect.

15:39.600 --> 15:42.320
And why are you over here with us again?

15:42.320 --> 15:43.300
Got it.

15:43.300 --> 15:45.210
I found Julie-san's feed.

15:45.910 --> 15:47.760
She was certainly active.

15:48.380 --> 15:50.760
Looks like she's having fun in every photo.

15:51.220 --> 15:52.470
Oh, here!

15:52.470 --> 15:54.310
This is the latte she drank...

15:55.460 --> 15:57.980
But nothing looks weird here.

15:59.190 --> 16:02.400
So the latte isn't giving us any clues.

16:02.400 --> 16:07.090
This is a problem! How'd the culprit 
get her to drink the poisoned latte?

16:11.160 --> 16:13.480
<i>He's sweating bullets 
and clutching his head...</i>

16:13.480 --> 16:16.750
<i>Somehow, I always thought he 
solved cases more easily than this.</i>

16:18.280 --> 16:22.460
No matter how I look at it, there's nothing 
wrong with the victim's latte. Right?

16:22.840 --> 16:26.240
<i>This isn't how I imagined Detective Isshiki.</i>

16:27.920 --> 16:29.940
You're drenched in sweat, Detective Isshiki.

16:29.940 --> 16:32.010
Here. A little refreshment on the house.

16:32.010 --> 16:33.010
What?

16:33.010 --> 16:34.870
A hot hand towel, grande size.

16:34.870 --> 16:35.970
That's a bath towel!

16:35.970 --> 16:38.810
Great, right? It'll steam up 
your glasses in an instant.

16:38.810 --> 16:40.400
Yeah, that's not great.

16:40.400 --> 16:43.020
And with our logo, 
it'll be a hit on social media!

16:43.020 --> 16:44.860
That is so not how you want to stand out.

16:45.730 --> 16:46.820
Exactly.

16:46.820 --> 16:49.510
That's the key, Detective Isshiki.

16:50.530 --> 16:52.950
When you pick the wrong way to stand out,

16:52.950 --> 16:54.990
you pick the wrong way in life, too.

16:57.700 --> 16:59.910
Wh-What are you talking about?

16:59.910 --> 17:01.620
<i>That pose means...</i>

17:02.210 --> 17:03.650
We've solved the mystery.

17:03.650 --> 17:04.370
What?

17:04.370 --> 17:06.050
You know who the perpetrator is?

17:06.050 --> 17:08.260
Huh? Y-Yeah, probably.

17:08.260 --> 17:11.170
I'm going to space out for a bit. 
Come keep an eye on me.

17:11.170 --> 17:12.300
S-Sure.

17:12.300 --> 17:14.220
<i>Right! I have to hear his deduction!</i>

17:17.580 --> 17:19.420
I have a favor to ask you.

17:19.420 --> 17:20.390
What?

17:20.390 --> 17:23.350
Could you hide anything in the kitchen 
with a blade for me?

17:23.670 --> 17:25.820
Is there a chance of a second murder?

17:25.820 --> 17:27.570
Um, yes.

17:27.570 --> 17:30.130
<i>Though it's the culprit who's in danger.</i>

17:34.490 --> 17:38.610
I would now like to solve 
the mystery of Julie-san's death.

17:38.610 --> 17:40.960
As I thought, this wasn't indiscriminate.

17:40.960 --> 17:43.170
Julie-san was murdered on purpose.

17:45.240 --> 17:46.340
But...

17:46.340 --> 17:49.470
Julie picked her latte at random.

17:49.470 --> 17:52.550
I thought there wasn't any way 
to make her drink a specific one.

17:52.550 --> 17:54.760
No, that was exactly the trick.

17:54.760 --> 17:57.900
The culprit knew Julie-san 
would pick the one in the back.

17:57.900 --> 17:58.610
What?

17:58.610 --> 18:01.390
The answer lies in Julie-san's social media.

18:01.860 --> 18:03.780
She's in the middle of every photo.

18:03.780 --> 18:08.110
She shot things in a way 
that drew attention to herself.

18:08.110 --> 18:13.440
Knowing she was like that, it was obvious 
that she'd choose most photogenic latte...

18:13.440 --> 18:15.390
none the wiser it was poisoned.

18:15.390 --> 18:19.270
But all three lattes had 
the same platypus on them.

18:19.270 --> 18:20.080
Yes.

18:20.560 --> 18:22.290
Up until a certain point.

18:23.810 --> 18:26.730
What the culprit did was incredibly simple.

18:26.730 --> 18:30.210
They just flicked a finger across
 the unpoisoned lattes.

18:31.880 --> 18:35.340
No one else would notice, 
and it only took a second.

18:37.300 --> 18:41.290
And it happened in the brief time 
they were being carried to the table.

18:41.290 --> 18:43.020
This photo is proof.

18:47.610 --> 18:50.290
Hayami-san, will you answer me this?

18:50.710 --> 18:52.820
How could two of those otherwise

18:52.820 --> 18:58.010
untouched lattes end up with just
 the eye of the design misshapen?

18:59.450 --> 19:01.160
The only one who could've done it...

19:01.160 --> 19:02.640
was you!

19:13.550 --> 19:16.800
But... But Julie was...

19:19.010 --> 19:23.300
She didn't just want to be 
the center of everything.

19:23.300 --> 19:26.600
She couldn't stand it when 
anyone else got attention.

19:26.600 --> 19:30.620
Even my boyfriend... 
The instant I got scouted by a talent agency,

19:30.620 --> 19:32.400
she stole him from me!

19:32.400 --> 19:34.090
That's why you...

19:34.090 --> 19:35.860
No matter how strong your hatred,

19:37.570 --> 19:40.270
killing someone is never the right answer!

19:41.990 --> 19:43.680
What would you know about—

19:43.680 --> 19:44.700
Bash your head in.

19:47.180 --> 19:49.780
Anyone who'd dismiss another's life

19:50.130 --> 19:52.840
has no right to live in this world.

19:53.250 --> 19:55.480
What is he saying?

19:55.480 --> 19:56.800
B-Bash her head...?

19:56.800 --> 19:58.490
Bash your head in.

20:01.220 --> 20:02.330
Yes...

20:33.540 --> 20:35.550
Ow!

20:35.550 --> 20:39.590
I reek of coffee. What is all this?

20:42.570 --> 20:44.590
Thank you, Toto.

20:57.980 --> 21:00.110
I'm really sorry!

21:00.110 --> 21:02.330
I broke your digital recorder.

21:02.330 --> 21:04.600
You were using that for your article, right?

21:04.600 --> 21:07.840
Yes, but it only had material
 from today on it.

21:07.840 --> 21:12.370
And it doesn't compare in the least to getting
to see a great detective's true nature.

21:12.370 --> 21:13.460
I'm perfectly satisfied.

21:13.880 --> 21:15.170
"True nature"?

21:15.170 --> 21:17.130
I realized something.

21:17.130 --> 21:20.990
When I saw you with your head in your hands, 
thinking over every detail...

21:21.300 --> 21:25.350
I saw that a great detective's brilliance 
isn't solving mysteries like magic.

21:25.350 --> 21:29.070
It's earnestly tackling 
everything with all their strength.

21:29.070 --> 21:32.560
I respect you even more now,
 Detective Isshiki.

21:32.560 --> 21:34.710
I hope we can work together in the future.

21:35.150 --> 21:36.650
I can't wait.

21:36.650 --> 21:37.570
<i>What the?</i>

21:37.570 --> 21:41.110
I'm delighted someone shares 
my opinion of Detective Isshiki's greatness.

21:41.110 --> 21:43.280
Here, I've made lattes for everyone.

21:43.280 --> 21:45.480
Carry them, won't you, Detective Isshiki?

21:45.870 --> 21:47.830
<b>Great news!</b>

21:45.870 --> 21:47.830
<b>Reporter connection</b>

21:45.870 --> 21:47.830
<b>acquired!</b>

21:45.870 --> 21:47.830
<i>I can't show her this!</i>

21:47.990 --> 21:49.680
These taste better when you mix them.

21:49.680 --> 21:52.170
Oh, thank you!

21:52.170 --> 21:55.340
Chikori-kun, if you're hungry,

21:55.340 --> 21:56.790
I'll order delivery for you.

21:56.790 --> 21:59.260
Cafés don't do that!

21:59.260 --> 22:01.520
Then you should treat her to home cooking.

22:01.520 --> 22:03.220
I want some too, so perfect timing.

22:03.220 --> 22:04.930
Seriously, what gives?

22:04.930 --> 22:08.070
I'll even drown your dishes 
in black sugar syrup for you!

22:08.070 --> 22:09.930
You <i>always</i> do that!
